invariant: INV-41
file: rsa_avx2_number.h
catches: rsa_avx2_model_test
reason: digits_to_words writes each digit's bits below the next word's
  edge and drops the bits that run into the next word, so the bytes
  rsa_avx2_public writes lose them wherever a digit runs into the next word.
  bin/rsa_avx2_model_test compares rsa_vp1_cpu under CH_CPU_AVX2 with
  rsa_vp1, and the chain's end with rsa_mont64_public.

--- old
        if (offset + bits > 64 && index + 1 <= word_count) {
            words[index + 1] |= digit >> (63 - offset) >> 1;
        }
--- new
